1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,160
A pole stands beside a school.

2
00:00:02,160 --> 00:00:04,680
Last week's photo looks normal.

3
00:00:04,680 --> 00:00:06,800
This week's photo looks different.

4
00:00:06,800 --> 00:00:09,800
Did the pole move or did the camera?

5
00:00:09,800 --> 00:00:12,800
The question is the problem behind SpanWitness.

6
00:00:12,800 --> 00:00:16,080
Reviewing separate photos makes changes hard to judge.

7
00:00:16,600 --> 00:00:21,080
Our approach keeps dated observations together by asset.

8
00:00:21,080 --> 00:00:23,960
It compares supported evidence and gives the next inspection

9
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:26,040
a clear purpose.

10
00:00:26,800 --> 00:00:29,400
Here is the working application.

11
00:00:29,400 --> 00:00:33,600
The page explains the problem before the technical details.

12
00:00:39,300 --> 00:00:42,900
The technical path starts with OpenCV5.

13
00:00:43,900 --> 00:00:47,300
It selects supported edges and fits the marked axis.

14
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:50,200
A bounded policy chooses the next action.

15
00:00:54,000 --> 00:00:59,040
A reviewer can inspect both images, add a note, and confirm a provisional review request.

16
00:01:12,400 --> 00:01:17,100
In Asset History, we compare a baseline with a later inspection.

17
00:01:17,100 --> 00:01:21,500
The demo uses original synthetic scenes and illustrative dates.

18
00:01:22,200 --> 00:01:25,400
Feature matching checks the background while excluding the pole.

19
00:01:26,500 --> 00:01:28,700
A bounded policy chooses the next action.

20
00:01:29,400 --> 00:01:32,000
Amazon Lambda runs the analysis.

21
00:01:33,200 --> 00:01:38,500
Private S3 stores images, DynamoDB store, observations and reviews.

22
00:01:44,200 --> 00:01:48,640
108 controlled history checks passed.

23
00:01:48,640 --> 00:01:53,660
Live cloud checks verified processing and saved record.

24
00:01:53,660 --> 00:01:57,080
These are not field accuracy results.

25
00:01:57,800 --> 00:02:00,820
This prototype does not diagnose cracks or predict

26
00:02:00,820 --> 00:02:03,460
a pole falling.

27
00:02:03,460 --> 00:02:06,420
The code and report explain the method.
